\section{The pieces}{

\code{\link[=sim_population]{sim_population()}} builds the dataset. You give it \code{n} and a list of named
variables, each made by a helper:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=sim_num]{sim_num()}} for numeric variables (normal), optionally bounded with \code{min}
and \code{max}
\item \code{\link[=sim_bin]{sim_bin()}} for binary variables, 0 or 1
\item \code{\link[=sim_count]{sim_count()}} for counts (Poisson)
\item \code{\link[=sim_cat]{sim_cat()}} for categories
\item \code{\link[=sim_within]{sim_within()}} to repeat each person across levels (pre/post, conditions)
}

Variables are built in the order you list them, and each one can use the
variables listed above it.
