\section{Two kinds of noise}{

In repeated-measures data, a variable listed \strong{above} \code{\link[=sim_within]{sim_within()}} is
drawn once per person (each person has their own value, shared across their
rows). It creates stable differences between people, so a person's
measurements are correlated. The \code{sd} of a variable listed \strong{below}
\code{\link[=sim_within]{sim_within()}} is a fresh error for every row.
}

\section{Output}{

The result has an \code{id} column (one value per person) followed by your
